      {
        "id": 73703,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-26T00:35:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Bum bag? I've never heard of that one.&nbsp; I just know that, here in the US, some people always ask the question \"Why is it called a fanny pack, when your fanny is in the back, and the fanny pack is worn in front?\"&nbsp; Given the UK definition of fanny, it makes more sense.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I believe they <em>were</em> originally worn at the back (especially by cyclists) but then people started wearing them at the front or side because that makes them less easy to pickpocket. So both names make total sense.</p>\n<p>Not that I've seen anyone wearing one since about 1992…</p>",
